course: dictionary
lesson: 2197
title: Council
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A council is a group of people chosen to make decisions or give advice. The word comes from the idea of people coming together to talk something over, and then deciding. «The council is the local government.» That means the council is the group that runs things for the people who live in a town or area.
explain: Councils look after everyday things. «Council tax is paid to the local council for local services such as bins, streetlights, roads and libraries.» So when you see a bin being emptied or a streetlight working, the council may have helped to make that happen.
explain: A school council works in a similar way. «Pupils vote for the school council.» The pupils on it share ideas and help make decisions for the whole school. Clue words like town, city, school and meeting show you what kind of council is being talked about.
fact: A council is a group of people chosen to make decisions or give advice.
fact: A school council is a group of pupils who share ideas and help make decisions for the school.
fact: The local council looks after things like bins, parks, libraries and roads.
fact: «Council tax» is paid to the local council. For example, «£110 a month is 12 × £110 = £1,320 a year.»
fact: Long ago, the council of the Zaporizhian Sich could elect its leaders and remove them, but only Cossack men had a voice in it.
exercise: «Council tax is paid to the local council for local services such as bins, streetlights, roads and libraries.» What does a council look after? | *Local things like bins, roads and libraries | Every person's birthday | Sweets and toys for the shops | Only the weather and the stars
exercise: «Pupils vote for the school council.» What is a school council? | *A group of pupils who share ideas and help make decisions for the school | A club for playing football at lunchtime | One pupil who makes every rule alone | A teacher's desk at the front of the class
exercise: «The council (rada) elected and could remove its leaders.» What could the council do with its leaders? | *Elect them and remove them | Build them a castle | Forget their names | Pay their council tax for them
test: Mia says a council is one person who makes all the rules alone. What is the mistake? | There is no mistake, she is right | *A council is a group of people, not just one person | A council is only for stars and planets | A council is a building where people eat lunch
test: «A town council meeting» is a meeting where people make decisions for the town. Which word tells you the meeting is about a town? | Meeting | Council | Decision, which is the last word of the phrase | *Town
exam: Tom says «council tax» pays for a holiday abroad. Is he right? | Yes, but only for people who are over sixty | *No, it pays for local things like bins, streetlights, roads and libraries | No, because it pays for the school council's sweets | Yes, it pays for holidays for everyone in the town
